    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The airflow theory makes sense, but the cooling isn't the only issue. Even with the ducts open, we're seeing these localized \"hot spots\" that appear and disappear without any clear mechanical or aero reason. It's almost like something is interfering with the friction coefficient in small, concentrated bursts. It feels less like a system failure and more like the braking system is just acting up or being sabotaged by some unseen variable. Is there anything in the metallurgy or the friction interface that could explain such sudden, mischievous-looking thermal spikes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
